# Files clasp must NOT push to the Apps Script project.
#
# ⚠️ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: .clasp.json has "rootDir": "." and
# "scriptExtensions": [".js"], so WITHOUT this file clasp uploads EVERY .js in
# the repo — including Node.js tooling. Apps Script evaluates every uploaded
# file at load time, so a single `require(...)` in a dev script throws
# "ReferenceError: require is not defined" and takes the WHOLE project down:
# no function runs, and the deployed web app stops serving. That happened once
# with tools/callable-surface.js. Anything that is not Apps Script runtime code
# belongs here.

# Node-only developer tooling (runs via `node`, never in Apps Script)
tools/**

# Docs and repo furniture
reference/**
migration-context/**
assets/**
.claude/**
*.md
*.py

# Version control / editor
.git/**
.gitignore
.claspignore
